{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"115624","commit":"5755968002086a78a66840628de4680f868407da","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The removal of `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand` from the optimizer rules list suggests a change in how limits are managed around `MvExpand`. This change should be well-documented and tested to ensure that the new logic correctly handles all cases, especially those involving nested operations and multiple limits.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-10015:10048-","promptId":"#9JB45","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10015,"endPos":10048,"startLine":177,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":177,"endLineOffset":45,"length":34}],"dstChanges":[]}]},{"comment":"The updated test cases reflect the new logic but could benefit from additional coverage of edge cases, such as when the limit is zero or negative, and when there are multiple `MvExpand` operations in a plan. It\u0027s also important to ensure that the expected output in the comments accurately reflects the changes made.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-52655:52673,52682:52711,52722:52774,52821:52876,53141:53175,53184:53230,53257:53270,53360:53401-52659:52704,52712:52761,52802:52875,53158:53162,53189:53231,53303:53348","promptId":"#PVEYY","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpac